class CrashFixSpringBall(PresetChoice):
    """
    Crash fix: Unequip Spring Ball bounce.

    Change the behaviour of how game crashes are handled. This feature can prevent a hardlock if any of the
    following bugs are triggered:
    - Spring Ball bounce: Triggered by pausing and unequipping Spring Ball at certain points in the middle of a
        neutral bounce.
    - Yapping Maw shinespark: If a Yapping Maw tries to grab Samus during a shinespark, followed by having no
        inputs held during the shinespark end.
    - Frame perfect pause, autoreserve: Having autoreserves trigger on the exact frame the screen finishes fading
        out while pausing.
    - X-Mode tile collision: Colliding with a solid tile during X-Mode.
    - Sprite overflow bug: Leaving a room with 32 sprites loaded.
    Individual customization options are available by clicking the gear button on the right.
    - Crash: When triggered, only the vanilla code will run. This will cause a hardlock of the game.
    - Death: When triggered, a dialog box will appear explaining the crash followed by triggering a death sequence
        / game-over, preventing the vanilla hardlock.
    - Warn: When triggered, a dialog box will appear explaining the crash but game play will continue after the
        dialog box is closed.
    - Silent: When triggered, no dialog box will appear and the game will continue as if the crash hadn't been
        triggered.
    Details
    The sprite overflow bug does not have a message box if set to death due to the bug happening in the door
    transition. For the same reason there is no warn option for this bug. Default behaviour for all presets other
    than crash is to silently fix the bug. If death is desired it can be manually enabled using the gear icon.
    In underwater physics, the Spring Ball bounce crash is triggered when Spring Ball is unequipped at any point
    while Samus is moving upward from the neutral bounce. In air physics, it happens when Spring Ball is
    unequipped on an exact frame when landing from the neutral bounce.

    'preset' keeps the value from the selected preset.
    """
    display_name = "Crash fix: Unequip Spring Ball bounce"
    path = "quality_of_life_settings.crash_fixes.spring_ball"
    option_crash = 1
    option_death = 2
    option_warn = 3
    option_silent = 4
    json_values = {1: 'Crash', 2: 'Death', 3: 'Warn', 4: 'Silent'}


