class DisableSpikesuit(PresetToggle):
    """
    Disable spikesuits.

    When this option is enabled, the game will be modified so that Samus is no longer able to obtain a flash suit
    via a glitched shinespark (by a spikesuit, slopespark, or R-mode knockback spark). Any logic that would
    require the use of these techniques will also be disabled.
    A flash suit is a glitched state in which Samus is in a permanent state of shinecharge. A flash suit may still
    be obtained by other methods, by interrupting a Crystal Flash using an elevator or R-mode stand-up.

    'preset' keeps the value from the selected preset.
    """
    display_name = "Disable spikesuits"
    path = "other_settings.disable_spikesuit"


class DisableBluesuit(PresetToggle):
    """
    Disable blue suits.

    When this option is enabled, the game is modified so that Samus is not able to obtain a blue suit, a glitched
    state in which Samus would remain permanently blue (e.g. after interrupting a shinespark with a Crystal Flash,
    an R-mode standup, Draygon kill, or Baby Metroid hug). Any logic that would require the use of a blue suit
    will also be disabled.

    'preset' keeps the value from the selected preset.
    """
    display_name = "Disable blue suits"
    path = "other_settings.disable_bluesuit"


class EnableMajorGlitches(PresetToggle):
    """
    Enable major glitches.

    When this option is enabled, the game no longer patches out major glitches:
    - "GT Code": holding A, B, X, and Y when entering Golden Torizo's Room grants the player 700 Energy, 300
        Reserve Energy, 100 Missiles, 20 Supers, 20 Power Bombs, and every unique item in the game except for
        Screw Attack and X-Ray.
    - Glitched beams: The player may equip Spazer and Plasma simultaneously, resulting in glitched effects when
        firing.
    - Out of bounds: Samus may move outside the rectangular bounds of the room without triggering death.
    Use this setting with caution, as major glitches may crash the game, corrupt the save file, or cause the game
    to become unbeatable. There is no guarantee that major glitches will behave the same as they do in the vanilla
    game.
    This option is always enabled when using "Ultra-low quality of life".

    'preset' keeps the value from the selected preset.
    """
    display_name = "Enable major glitches"
    path = "other_settings.enable_major_glitches"


class Savestate(PresetChoice):
    """
    Enable savestates.

    This in-game save state option allows creating at most one save state at a time. A save state can be loaded an
    unlimited amount of times. Any save state is cleared automatically by a regular save (at a save station or the
    Ship).
    - Unlimited: A save state can be created at any time.
    - Limited: A save state can be created only once, until refreshed by a regular save or load.
    Compared to emulator/platform-based save states, the in-game save state option has some advantages:
    - Map tile progress is maintained.
    - Music continues uninterrupted if the track is unchanged.
    - Item collection times and other stats are preserved.
    - The fact that save states are cleared by regular saves can help prevent accidental loads.
    - The "Limited" option, if enabled, forces strategic use of save states.
    - It works for some platforms (e.g FXPAK) that would otherwise be unsupported.
    This feature requires 256KB SRAM; FXPAK and most modern emulators support this configuration.

    'preset' keeps the value from the selected preset.
    """
    display_name = "Enable savestates"
    path = "other_settings.savestate"
    option_no = 1
    option_limited = 2
    option_unlimited = 3
    json_values = {1: 'No', 2: 'Limited', 3: 'Unlimited'}


class RaceMode(PresetToggle):
    """
    Race mode.

    When set to "Yes", spoiler data is initially locked. The creator of the seed can unlock the spoiler data, at
    which point it will become viewable to everyone, and the timestamp when the spoiler data was unlocked will be
    shown on seed page.
    The seed creator will need to use the same device and browser to unlock the spoiler data as what they used to
    create it (as the ability to unlock the data depends on a small random token in browser-local storage).

    'preset' keeps the value from the selected preset.
    """
    display_name = "Race mode"
    path = "other_settings.race_mode"


